<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Empty product VINTF manifest for qalos emulator.

  AOSP 15's vintffm frozen-manifest check (build/make/target/product/vintf/
  check_vintf_all.mk, invoked during the final packaging step at
  out/target/product/<product>/obj/PACKAGING/check_vintf_all_intermediates/
  vintffm.log) walks the staged system/product/etc/vintf/manifest.xml. If
  the file is missing, the check fails with NAME_NOT_FOUND and aborts the
  build before any of the .img files are sealed, even when the actual
  compilation has succeeded.

  qalos inherits AOSP's aosp_x86_64 product, which does not declare any
  product-shipped HALs of its own (the HALs all live in vendor/ via the
  generic x86_64 vendor tree). The product manifest is therefore empty.

  An empty <manifest> element with type="device" is the canonical
  "no product-shipped HALs" answer. **AOSP 15's vintf schema only accepts
  type="device" or type="framework" (see
  system/libvintf/include/vintf/SchemaType.h).** Earlier we shipped
  type="product" and assemble_vintf rejected it with "unknown format".
  type="device" with no <hal> entries is what AOSP's own empty
  product manifests use. vintffm sees the file, finds no HAL entries
  to verify against the level-5 frozen matrix, and the check passes.

  Wired by PRODUCT_MANIFEST_FILES in device/qalos/qalos_emulator/device.mk.
  AOSP 15's build system (system/libhidl/vintfdata/Android.mk) consumes
  this list and creates a prebuilt module that assembles the entries via
  assemble_vintf and installs at system/product/etc/vintf/manifest.xml
  (LOCAL_PRODUCT_MODULE=true, LOCAL_MODULE_RELATIVE_PATH := vintf).
  This is the canonical AOSP 15 mechanism for shipping a product
  manifest; PRODUCT_COPY_FILES for VINTF manifests is rejected by
  build/make/core/Makefile.
-->
<manifest version="1.0" type="device">
</manifest>
